# miracle: S1 defines it as a violation of the laws of nature, while S3 and S5 pick miracles out as what has never been observed in the course of nature. I read S3 and S5 as a test for spotting the same thing, not a second sense.
# uniform: critics charge that "uniform experience" means all past observation in one place and all experience, including the reported miracle, in another. I read the text as using "no contrary case has been observed" throughout. I was unsure here.
